  "other_facts": "Direct antiglobulin test (DAT) is considered an important test in identifying newborns suspected to have HDN. Data were obtained from patients' electronic hospital files, transfusion medicine databases, and medical birth records. 176 neonates had a positive DAT result. Etiology of DAT positivity: ABO-incompatibility 59.1%, Rh incompatibility 13.8%, minor blood group incompatibility and other RBC-related antibodies 10.1%, unspecified etiology 17%. ABO-incompatibility was also the major reason for HDN diagnosis. Treatment rates among DAT-positive neonates: phototherapy 86.8%, exchange transfusion (ET) 32.7%, intravenous immunoglobulin (IVIG) 17.6%. Rare causes of DAT positivity include antibodies passively acquired from mothers in the context of alloimmunizations or using drugs.",
